## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required relationship |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Cardamom capsule, beta-pinene edge, black pepper, aldehydic rind | Linalyl/linalool seam and premium lavender body | First dry cedar and coumarin shadows | Cardamom must precede and organize the citrus |
| 5–45 min | Cold pod shell narrows | Lavender hinge exposes warm seed through dihydrojasmone, Jessemal, clary, Leafovert, and Dynascone | Coumarin/Tonkarome, damascenone, heliotropal, immortelle straw, and bark shadow | Warmth must feel like the inside of the same pod |
| 45 min–3 h | Aromatic seed residue | Violet/root cloth and warm fatty-floral stitches | Cedar/vetiver verticals and separated sandalwood chamber | Tailoring shapes cardamom; it does not become lipstick iris or leather |
| 3–8 h+ | Dry aromatic grain | Coumarinic wood and creamy skin | Mineral pressure and long dry contour | The base must recall cardamom/lavender through ester, seed, cloth, and wood relations |

All temporal language above is design intent, not observed evolution.

